{"key": "fight_title",
    "value": "Canelo Álvarez vs. Billy Joe Saunders, billed as 'Face the Fearless', a unification super middleweight bout held on May 8, 2021, at AT&T Stadium in Arlington, Texas."
  }

{"key": "fighters",
    "value": "Canelo Álvarez (Mexico, 5'8\", orthodox, 55-1-2, 37 KOs, WBA (Super), WBC, The Ring titles) vs. Billy Joe Saunders (England, 5'11\", southpaw, 30-0, 14 KOs, WBO champion)."
  }

{"key": "background",
    "value": "Originally scheduled for May 2, 2020, in Las Vegas, the fight was postponed due to the COVID-19 pandemic. Canelo filed a lawsuit against DAZN and Oscar De La Hoya over unpaid contract amounts, leading to his release from Golden Boy Promotions in November 2020. Saunders withdrew from the September 2020 date due to unavailability."
  }

{"key": "pre-fight_events",
    "value": "After becoming a free agent, Canelo defeated Callum Smith in December 2020 and Avni Yıldırım in February 2021, both to retain his unified titles. An agreement to face Saunders was reached before the Yıldırım fight."
  }
